  "problem": "On which of the following intervals can the extreme value theorem be applied to the function $y={log}_{2}\u2061(x-2)?$  \n\n- $[-1,1]$\n- $[2,3)$\n- $[3,4]$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[-1,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because $y={log}_{2}\u2061(x-2)$ is not defined anywhere in this interval. Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[2,3)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[3,4]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[3,4].$  Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
